Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(mcp): locate_part takes mate ids by the one pick rule

The audit of #692 after #705/#709 found one picker left outside the
rule: MCP locate_part parsed its mate ids without pick::check_pickable,
so a vertex along a round rim or inside a face became a mate point. It
now runs the same check as every other MCP pick. The user guide gets a
"What a click picks" section; centre picks wait for #759.

Pinned by mcp_pick::locate_part_refuses_a_mate_point_no_click_could_pick.

Refs #692

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
